## Essential grammatical elements in ggplot2: stats

### Working with stat()


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data=exam_data,
       aes(y = MATHS, x= GENDER)) +
  geom_boxplot()
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](HO_Ex1_submission_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-20-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Working with stat: the stat_summary() method


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data=exam_data,
       aes(y = MATHS, x= GENDER)) +
  geom_boxplot() +
  stat_summary(geom = "point",
               fun = "mean",
               colour ="red",
               size=4)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](HO_Ex1_submission_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-21-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Working with stat: the geom() method


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data=exam_data,
       aes(y = MATHS, x= GENDER)) +
  geom_boxplot() +
  geom_point(stat="summary",
             fun="mean",
             colour="red",
             size=4)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](HO_Ex1_submission_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-22-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Adding a best-fit curve to a scatterplot


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggplot(data=exam_data,
       aes(x= MATHS, y=ENGLISH)) +
  geom_point() +
  geom_smooth(size=0.5)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](HO_Ex1_submission_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-23-1.png){width=672}
